==Enemy==
The Red Malice is tanky, moves quickly, has a very fast attack rate and causes knockback on hit. However, he still has 10 knockbacks and lower range which makes it easier for your units to hold him back if you can whittle his health quickly.

==Strategy==
Use powerful, long-ranged cats like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], or [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]]. His knockback ability is a double-edged sword, as while it helps him to push, the fact that it disables hitboxes for a few frames mean other enemies can miss, so [[:Category:Cats with Knockback Immunity|knockback immune]] [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] may not be the best idea. Unless he is weakened or frozen, it also isn't recommended to use rushers such as [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] or Awakened Bahamut Cat against him, as his damage is usually sufficient to knock them back with each hit, and his fast attack rate will likely prevent them from ever hitting him, even without support.

